    "solution": "Wait for the ram to break the upper masonry stop and become dazed on the horizontal bridge. Cut the brass hub from the eastern ledge: the bridge folds up, delivering that same enemy to the lower lane. Climb its new wall and dash left over the upper workshop, then drop through the western chute. Collect the lower tally and approach the sealed low passage. The ram sees you from the other side and breaks its second wall. Retreat to the raised western perch until it recovers and walks away, then follow through the opened passage. In the open arena, let it turn and answer its next charge with a parry beneath the return balcony. Jump toward its dazed body, hold Jump while cutting Down for a lofted pogo, then dash Up to the broad balcony. Rest there, move left of the folded arm, jump and climb that same wall from its other face. Walk right along the broad upper exit gallery.",
    "nearestExisting": "B27 lets a ram replace one shield; B11 makes a bridge become a stair. Here transforming the bridge transports a living breaching tool into an otherwise sealed chamber, and approach side reverses its useful job.",
    "novelty": "A floor changes not only the knight route but the enemy route. The ram must first be delivered to another altitude; the knight then reaches its opposite side to use it again. The folded floor becomes the ascent supported by that same ram.",
